From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] dropbear: update to 2026.94
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Replace the 2025.89 cherry-picks from 0029 and 0042 with dropbear
2026.94, using OpenWrt main's package (feb8ac5e7e: Makefile, Config.in
and the refreshed 100 to 901 patches). On top of it, two upstream
commits newer than 2026.94 and one local fix:

  001 59870ad4 Enforce channel max packet > 0
  002 17549ea6 Fix terminal escaping in scp
  003 local    scp: keep the error marker in run_err()

002 passes the whole remote error message, including its leading 0x01
"recoverable error" byte, through cleantext(), which drops that byte.
The peer then sees an unmarked protocol line and a single missing file
aborts a batch transfer. 003 cleans only the text after the marker and
strips whitespace there too, so a newline in a remote filename cannot
split the protocol line.

2026.94 adds fixes that the cherry-picks never carried. Among them:
the curve25519 S < L and y < p checks (CVE-2026-3706), a limit on
public key queries per session, no signals under a forced command or
without dropped privileges, RSA exponent blinding, O_NOFOLLOW for scp
and dropbearkey output files, a 300-line authorized_keys cap, an
FD_SET overflow check and an ECDSA curve identifier out-of-bounds read.
910-signkey is dropped; OpenWrt main removed it as obsolete
(f6cc96990a), since 2026.92 fixed it upstream.

files/dropbear.init and files/dropbear.failsafe stay at the 25.12
versions. Main's versions add host-key type detection, a
MaxSessionDuration option and VRF support (procd vrf), none of which
2026.94 requires. ECDSA stays off through the explicit
"# CONFIG_DROPBEAR_ECDSA is not set" in .config, despite main's new
default. The new MAX_PUBKEY_QUERIES (15) and DEFAULT_MAX_DURATION (0)
options come from Config.in defaults through make defconfig.

